-- title:
--   Two-sided pools of étale blocks in the smooth locus, p=2
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M$ a nonzero modulus with $p \mid M$ and $p^2 \nmid M$, let $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ be a subgroup containing every unit whose image under the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$ is trivial, and assume the Laurent series `jqModC ℚ` of $j$ lies in the field `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ ⊤` generated by ratios of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms of full level. Let $\mathfrak{X}$ be a datum `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj`, which packages the proper, flat, integral and normal two-chart integral model `X p (ΓM M H) hj` of $X_H(M)$ over `Spec (R p)` together with its open smooth locus `𝔛.smoothLocus`, the section `𝔛.εinf`, a self-isomorphism `𝔛.w`, and an identification `𝔛.eeta` of its base change to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with a curve model `𝔛.Meta` having function field `xHFunctionFieldBar M H`. Let $\theta$ be a $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-algebra automorphism of `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` such that whenever $f$ in that field and $u$ in `xHFunctionFieldBar (M / p) (infSubgroup p M H hpM)` have the same Laurent series, $\theta f$ has Laurent series `qExpand _ p` applied to that of $u$, i.e. the substitution $q \mapsto q^{p}$; assume further (`hwgen`) that for any two $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points $y, y'$ of `𝔛.Meta.C` over the base, equality of $y'$ followed by `𝔛.eeta`, the first projection and `𝔛.w.hom` with $y$ followed by `𝔛.eeta` and that projection forces `𝔛.Meta.pointEquivPlace y'` to be the translate of `𝔛.Meta.pointEquivPlace y` by the semilinear automorphism `SemilinearAut.ofAlgAut θ`. Finally let $\mathfrak{p}$ be a point of `PrimeSpectrum (R p)` with nonzero prime ideal, assume $p = 2$, and let $A_0, B_0, n_0$ be naturals. Then there exist $f \in R p$ with $f \notin \mathfrak{p}$, a bound $b$, and $N_1, N_2$ with $A_0 b^{n_0} + B_0 < N_1, N_2$, a commutative ring $R'$ that is an `R p`- and `Localization.Away f`-algebra in a scalar tower, module-finite, étale and faithfully flat over `Localization.Away f`, and two families of finite étale `Localization.Away f`-algebras $B_i$ ($i \in \mathrm{Fin}\,N_1$) and $B'_i$ ($i \in \mathrm{Fin}\,N_2$) with degrees $\deg i, \deg' i \in [1, b]$, $R'$-algebra isomorphisms $R' \otimes B_i \cong R'^{\deg i}$ and $R' \otimes B'_i \cong R'^{\deg' i}$, and closed immersions $z_i \colon \operatorname{Spec} B_i \to \mathfrak{X} \times_{R p} \mathrm{Localization.Away}\,f$ and $z'_i$ likewise, such that: each $z_i$ and each $z'_i$ is a morphism over `Localization.Away f`; the images of all $z_i$ and $z'_i$ lie in the preimage of `𝔛.smoothLocus` under the first projection; the images of the $z_i$ are pairwise disjoint, those of the $z'_i$ are pairwise disjoint, and no $z_i$-image meets a $z'_j$-image; some $\deg' j \le 1$; for every algebraically closed field $k$ and every $s \colon \operatorname{Spec} k \to \operatorname{Spec}(\mathrm{Localization.Away}\,f)$ and every $i$, the part of the image of $z_i$ in the fibre lies in the connected component, within the preimage of `𝔛.smoothLocus`, of the point of the fibre determined by the base change of `𝔛.εinf`; and for every such $k$, $s$ and $i$, if the fibre over $s$ is not smooth then the part of the image of $z'_i$ in it lies in the preimage of `𝔛.smoothLocus` with that connected component removed.
--
--   This supplies, at the closed prime of `R p` and in the case $p = 2$, two disjoint families ("pools") of rational finite étale blocks of bounded degree inside the smooth locus of the Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_H(M)$ at a prime exactly dividing the level, one family concentrated in the cuspidal component of each non-smooth geometric fibre and the other avoiding it, with a block of degree one in the second family and with the number of blocks exceeding a prescribed polynomial bound $A_0 b^{n_0} + B_0$. It is used by the corresponding statement at the generic prime and by the combined pools statement, which feed the relative Picard and Néron model computations for these models.
